G3D: GImage::Format and the 4-argument GImage::resolveFormat as in PLAYER: upstream G3D's PPM_BINARY/
PPM_ASCII values and PPM/PGM/PBM, "TRUEVISION-XFILE" detection (g3d SVN r30 G3D.lib/include/G3D/GImage.h,
source/GImage.cpp), followed by the fork's PVR and DDS checks. PLAYER evidence, resolveFormat 0x009df070
(951 bytes): pushes "PPM" 0x00bbd604, "PGM" 0x00bbd600, "PBM" 0x00bbd5fc, compares "P6"/"P5"/"P3"/
"P2"/"P1", "TRUEVISION-XFILE" 0x00bbd5e8, then data+0x2c "PVR" -> returns 11 and "DDS" -> 10, falling
through to 9 (UNKNOWN); PPM_BINARY is 6, PPM_ASCII 7. So the enum is upstream's with the fork's DDS, PVR
after UNKNOWN. resolveFormat 0x009df070 and stringToFormat 0x009deea0 become identical.

